A||||4||My7Fieros||CAN YOU BELIEVE THIS!?||||10||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||07-01-2000||03:13 AM||||Well a good friend of mine called me the other day. He is interested in Fieros since his brother and myself have so many of them, and of course, since we use his garage and driveway to work and store all the ones in need of work. He said he found a Fiero at a local shop in the Chinatown area here in Memphis. He wanted us to come see if it was worth buying.<BR>So we go and look at it. Its an 87 Gt, burgandy/grey w/every available option except rear window defrost (which in my opinion is kinda dumb, jeez, the rear window heats up in no time do to the engine!)including premium sound w/ subwoofer. The engine had been dropped (correctly, believe it or not) do to overheating and needing a new head gasket. <BR>The car is in super great shape other than that. "The guy wants 400 for it" he said.."should I get it, seeing how you two can fix/rebuild the engine if needed".<BR>Hell yes! I told him. Well...the next day he calls and stated he bought the car. Cool! Looks like Ive got another project on my hands! :-)<BR>Oh yeah, by the way, when he went to get it, the guy at the shop said, "two hundred dolla...just take, it big headache, I want it gone!"...<BR>200 bucks! Now my only regret is that I didnt buy it!<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||07-01-2000||04:38 AM||||Hot damn! Maybe you should tell your friend you'll buy it from <I>him</I> for $400 dollars so he'll walk away with a 100% profit!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||07-01-2000||05:13 AM||||This Fiero is the same as mine. I would've paid $500.00 for it just for PARTS!||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||07-01-2000||12:22 PM||||An 87 fiero GT around here in New England would easily sell for $3000 and up for one in nice shape. The real nice ones in virgin form sell for $4000 and up. Last week I looked at a red 88 Formula with T-tops. The guy was asking $5800 for the dam thing and it was in ruff shape. The seals were all shot, the passenger side door was misaligned and it was a different color than the rest of the car because of an accident. The rear bumper had scuffs on it and a crappy paint fix were you could see a tape line shaped like a box, the seat had a rip in it on the drivers side. From what I could see through the homemade tint job on the windows it had 23,000 miles on it and new Monroe shocks and struts underneath the car. It was an automatic too.<P>Two weeks ago I looked at an 87 GT loaded in OK shape from what I could see from the street. The sign said asking $5800, mileage 123,000 miles. The front side marker light was hanging out of it and the paint on the front bumper was peeling a little.<P> I paid $3900 for my formula with 48,000 miles on it, but the guy had all the service records for it from day one and it was in excellent shape, especially the interior. He gave me a GM service manual, some factory brochures, and some other stuff like a front license plate holder in the plastic and a glove box, which I sold. <P>Your brother is lucky to find a deal like that!<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||olympic||07-01-2000||05:00 PM||||  I've also noticed that the prices of Fiero's here in Canada are going up....fast!!!||||reg||1
